    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261-a2">

                <pb facs="0624" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in dispatch No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kapena to Mr.
                            Comly.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of this date submitting to my consideration “the question
                    whether the tariff collected by the Hawaiian custom-house upon all cotton
                    manufactured into clothing, ‘the same being the growth, manufacture, or produce
                    of the United States,’ is not in contravention of Article II of the reciprocity
                    treaty.”</p>
                <p>I have forwarded a copy of your dispatch to His Excellency S. K. Kaai, minister
                    of finance, and await his answer, in order that I may fully reply to the
                    question embraced in your letter now acknowledged.</p>
                <p>With the highest respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN M. KAPENA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">James M. Comly</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister Resident.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
